Continuation — Phase 17 gate rerun and corrections, 2026-10-13 UTC:
- The first five-crate locked test rerun exposed a race in `async_active_listener_is_owned_panic_isolated_and_cancelled_on_shutdown`: the test checked a `spawn_blocking` callback's drop immediately after joining the event worker, although shutdown cancellation can finish just after that join. Added a drop notification and one-second bounded wait; the focused test passed and the full suite then passed.
- The first Maven verification found `ConsumerRunningInfo` fixture drift. Its Java fixture used `Set.of`, whose iteration order varied across JVM runs; changed the fixture input to `LinkedHashSet` with fixed insertion order. `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` then passed, including the 32-scenario manifest and Rust/Java cross-decodes (53 headers, 14 typed bodies).
- PASS after these corrections: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol -p rocketmq-classic-core -p rocketmq-classic-remoting -p rocketmq-classic-consumer -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked`; strict `cargo clippy` for the same crates with all targets/features and `-D warnings`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; and `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`.
- Updated the Phase 17 matrix with these results. Phase 17 still needs all-thread `jstackEnable` parity outside macOS and its logical commits/phase close; Phase 19 Broker query evidence is deferred as planned. Phase 18 remains unstarted.
